          "quote": "iii) within [*] Days after expiration or termination of this Agreement, MSL shall return to IBM all copies of IBM Product documentation and all copies of any IBM confidential documents, discs, tapes and other media materials containing IBM confidential information of IBM.",
          "rationale": "Exit protection exists and runs in our favour. Section 5.2(a)(ii) obliges MSL to \"assist in the transfer of MSL responsibilities and Products as described in Attachment 1: Statement Of Work, to IBM or to another party that IBM designates\" on expiry or termination for default, with no cap on the assistance window (better for us than the 6-month/90-day benchmarks), and 5.2(a)(iii) requires return of all IBM documentation and all discs, tapes and media containing IBM confidential information within a defined period after termination. Attachment 6 Section 3(a) adds return of master media plus signed written certification of compliance, and Section 13.2(c) lets IBM demand immediate return of confidential information at any time during the term. Nothing permits MSL to withhold or immediately destroy IBM data, so there is no walk-away exposure. Minor points noted only: the return period in 5.2(a)(iii) is redacted so we cannot confirm it is 30 days or less, deletion-and-certification is expressed only for the Attachment 6 MS Software Images rather than all IBM data, and there is no express machine-readable format requirement. These are sub-elements short of the preferred wording and do not warrant a redline.",
